## 3.  Extending the API

| Feature | How to Add |
|---------|------------|
| **Validation** | `@Valid` + `javax.validation` constraints (`@NotBlank`, `@Size`) on DTOs and a `MethodArgumentNotValidException` handler. |
| **DTOs & Mapping** | Create separate `BookDto` objects and use a mapper (e.g., MapStruct or ModelMapper) to convert between entity and DTO. |
| **Pagination** | `Pageable` and `Page<T>` in the repository and controller (`/api/books?page=0&size=20`). |
| **Security** | Add `spring-boot-starter-security`; configure in-memory or JWT auth. |
| **Swagger/OpenAPI** | Add `springdoc-openapi-starter-webmvc-ui` to automatically generate UI. |
| **Database** | Replace H2 with MySQL/PostgreSQL; update `application.yml` datasource. |
| **Unit / Integration Tests** | Use `@SpringBootTest` and `MockMvc` to test controllers; use `@DataJpaTest` for repository tests. |
| **Docker** | Add a simple `Dockerfile` (`FROM eclipse-temurin:17-jre-alpine`) and build an image. |
| **CI/CD** | Configure GitHub Actions / GitLab CI to run tests and build the JAR. |

