## 5.  Quick Code Snapshot (One‑File)

If you’re looking for the *absolute minimal* example that you can paste into a single file and run, here it is:

```java
// BookApi.java
package com.example;

import org.springframework.boot.*;
import org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.*;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.*;
import org.springframework.data.jpa.repository.*;
import jakarta.persistence.*;
import java.util.*;

@SpringBootApplication
public class BookApi {
    public static void main(String[] args) { SpringApplication.run(BookApi.class, args); }

    @Entity class Book { @Id @GeneratedValue Long id; String title, author; int year; Book() {} Book(String t,String a,int y){title=t;author=a;year=y;} }
    interface BookRepository extends JpaRepository<Book,Long> {}
    @RestController @RequestMapping("/api/books")
    class BookController {
        private final BookRepository repo;
        BookController(BookRepository r){this.repo=r;}
        @GetMapping List<Book> all(){return repo.findAll();}
        @PostMapping Book create(@RequestBody Book b){return repo.save(b);}
        @GetMapping("/{id}") Book get(@PathVariable Long id){return repo.findById(id).orElseThrow();}
        @PutMapping("/{id}") Book update(@PathVariable Long id,@RequestBody Book b){return repo.findById(id).map(e->{e.title=b.title;e.author=b.author;e.year=b.year;return repo.save(e);}).orElseThrow();}
        @DeleteMapping("/{id}") void delete(@PathVariable Long id){repo.deleteById(id);}
    }
}
```

Compile & run:

```bash
$ javac -cp ~/.m2/repository/org/springframework/boot/spring-boot-starter-web/3.3.0/spring-boot-starter-web-3.3.0.jar:... BookApi.java
$ java -cp .:... com.example.BookApi
```

*This is just for a quick demo; for anything beyond trivial, stick with the multi‑class structure above.*

